The page combines several results normally credited after 1866:
- the functional equation of general Dirichlet L-series mod q with Gauss-sum normalization (Hurwitz 1882);
- the explicit formula for psi(x) with the exact constant -log 2pi and the term -1/2 log(1-x^-2), plus an independent check of that constant through zeta'(2)/zeta(2) and Hadamard-type sums over zeros (von Mangoldt 1895);
- the start of the Laplace explicit formula for sum Lambda(n)e^{-ny} (Hardy-Littlewood).
Parts of Riemann's Nachlass, e.g. the zero computations and possibly the value 0.0230957, are partly known to historians. I am unsure how much of the L-function and psi(x) material has been published. Hence a notable but not top score.
